-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- 0446 — THE REAL STRAITS ARE OPEN: MESSINA, THE GREAT BELT, BANGKA, SURABAYA'S FAIRWAY (owner row 352, 2026-11-15)
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- PART A is GENERATED by scripts/build-straits.mjs from a world image of the applied chain (new raster
-- c25da58208c788b3a9b7caecd64ce0be, coast mask public/coast/mask.json); PART B (below the mark) by
-- scripts/build-sea-legs-migration.mjs --append. Do not hand-edit: re-run the generators and cut a NEW migration.
--
-- THE OWNER: the fix over-corrected. Messina to Zakynthos is 630 nm where it was 291: the course goes
-- round Sicily, not through the Strait of Messina, "a real, wide strait that ships must be able to pass".
--
-- ── THE CAUSE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- 0440 took every course off the land the chart draws, and 0441 ended the approach allowance (a course
-- could run over raster land within 25 nm of a harbour). Both were right. But both had been standing in
-- for real straits that the 0.25-degree raster (Natural Earth 1:110m) closes:
--   * the Strait of Messina: the raster joins Sicily to Calabria. Messina's roadstead lay 14 nm off in the
--     Tyrrhenian, and its courses south and east crossed the toe of Calabria inside the old allowance.
--     No other harbour's course ever passed the strait: Naples to Zakynthos was always round Sicily;
--   * the western fairway of Surabaya: the raster has no Madura and closes the fairway's cell; the old
--     course from the Java Sea crossed the island's west end;
--   * the Great Belt: the raster has no Funen and closes one cell of open water west of Zealand; the old
--     course crossed Funen's Hindsholm, the re-sailed one went by the Sound;
--   * the Bangka strait: the raster has no Bangka and draws Sumatra across the strait's southern half; the
--     old course crossed the island, the re-sailed one went east of it.
-- The audit of every harbour pair (docs/dev-log/2026-11-16-straits.md) found these four and no other
-- strait closed by 0440 or 0441.
--
-- ── 1. THE CHARTED CHANNELS (scripts/sea-grid.mjs CHANNELS, `charted: true`) ──────────────────────
--   6 raster cell(s) open, each drawn water on the chart:
--     great-belt   cell 198043 (55.625, 10.875)
--     messina      cell 297422 (38.375, 15.625)
--     messina      cell 298862 (38.125, 15.625)
--     bangka       cell 533943 (-2.625, 105.875)
--     bangka       cell 535383 (-2.875, 105.875)
--     surabaya     cell 559890 (-7.125, 112.625)
--   public.sea_cells names 6 of them after the nearest named water (0040, as 0091 and 0440 did);
--   voyage.channels gains the 4 channels. The land the chart draws inside these cells stays land: the coast
--   mask lists it and the audit counts it. Messina and Surabaya's fairway are drawn narrower than the course
--   author's 1.5-nm grid can follow, so the fine cells their own lines run through are water in the mask
--   (`fairway`, scripts/build-coast-mask.mjs); each line is drawn water at every 0.25 nm.
--
-- ── 2. THE ROADSTEADS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--   A quay that now stands in a charted cell lies on that channel (voyage.water_roadstead's own rule, 0085).
--   1 harbour(s) change their roadstead:
--     MES 38.375, 15.375 -> 38.185, 15.592 (on messina; 2.00 nm off the quay)
--   0 of them by 0440's rule for a roadstead on drawn land or in a pocket (voyage.drawn_roadsteads).
--
-- ── 3. THE COURSES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--   1670 distinct stored courses read (the chain's world and production's, exported read only at
--   2026-11-15T14:53:42.890595+00:00). 38 re-sailed: every course to or from a changed roadstead, every course over
--   drawn land (0), and every course that the course author's own search now takes through an opened strait
--   more than 15 nm and 3 % shorter (21). 0 still cross. With each one backwards: 46 replacements.
--   Rewritten by md5(course::text), as 0440 and 0441 did: public.npc_courses (25 of 1141 on the chain's world),
--   public.standing_route_stops (77 of 3350), public.npc_coast_courses (0 of 12), a cargo circuit's and a
--   navy patrol's frozen pieces either way round, the zones memo; then public.sea_leg_asks_keep().
--   On prod at the export: lanes 30 of 1351, route stops 70 of 2538, coast courses 0.
--   Voyages already sailing finish their course (decided by default, as 0440).
--
-- budget: no table, no cron job, no autovacuum or fillfactor change. 6 bits of the one raster row; 4 rows of
-- voyage.channels; 1 sea_reaches rows; the lanes, route stops and cargo legs that hold a replaced course.
-- ROLLBACK (forward, owner only): scripts/ops/harness/straits/rollback-0446.sql.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

-- ── 0. THE CONTROLS, BEFORE: each strait's own line, every sample read, is land ────────────────
do $$
begin
  if to_regprocedure('public.sea_leg_asks_keep()') is null or to_regclass('voyage.drawn_roadsteads') is null then
    raise exception '0446 refuses: 0440 (the drawn roadsteads) or 0442 (the pair table''s step) is not in this world';
  end if;
  if voyage.path_refusal('[[38.4,15.48],[38.32,15.62],[38.29,15.67],[38.272,15.695],[38.257,15.66],[38.245,15.62],[38.23,15.6],[38.2,15.595],[38.175,15.59],[38.15,15.585],[38.1,15.57],[38.05,15.56],[38.01,15.56],[37.97,15.57]]'::jsonb, 38.4, 15.48, 37.97, 15.57, 0, 0, 0) is null then
    raise exception '0446 self-assert FAIL: messina is water before its cells open, so its control proves nothing';
  end if;
  if voyage.path_refusal('[[55.47,10.88],[55.56,10.85],[55.66,10.83],[55.74,10.82],[55.8,10.8]]'::jsonb, 55.47, 10.88, 55.8, 10.8, 0, 0, 0) is null then
    raise exception '0446 self-assert FAIL: great-belt is water before its cells open, so its control proves nothing';
  end if;
  if voyage.path_refusal('[[-2.4,105.76],[-2.55,105.76],[-2.7,105.83],[-2.85,105.86],[-2.92,105.95],[-2.97,106.1]]'::jsonb, -2.4, 105.76, -2.97, 106.1, 0, 0, 0) is null then
    raise exception '0446 self-assert FAIL: bangka is water before its cells open, so its control proves nothing';
  end if;
  if voyage.path_refusal('[[-6.95,112.7],[-7,112.7],[-7.03,112.67],[-7.045,112.68],[-7.056,112.675],[-7.07,112.66],[-7.11,112.67],[-7.135,112.68],[-7.155,112.7],[-7.18,112.715],[-7.195,112.76],[-7.195,112.8]]'::jsonb, -6.95, 112.7, -7.195, 112.8, 0, 0, 0) is null then
    raise exception '0446 self-assert FAIL: surabaya is water before its cells open, so its control proves nothing';
  end if;
end
$$;

